quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  2,38,"We said: ‘Go down hence all! When the guidance comes to you from Me, those who follow My guidance shall have no fear, nor shall they grieve."
  2,39,"However, those who deny and reject Our revelations shall be the heirs of Hell, and they shall abide in it forever.’"
  2,40,"O Children of Israel! Remember My blessing I bestowed upon you, and fulfil My covenant (so that) I may fulfil your covenant. And fear Me alone."
  2,41,"Believe in (the Book) that I have revealed (to My Messenger Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him), which verifies (the Scriptures) that are with you. And do not be the first to deny it, and do not sell My revelations for a paltry gain. And fear Me alone."
  2,42,"Do not confound truth with falsehood, nor hide the truth while you know (it)."
  2,43,"Establish the prayers, pay the alms due and bow down with those who bow down (in worship)."
  2,44,"Would you enjoin righteousness on others and neglect yourselves, even though you recite the Scripture? Do you not then understand?"
  2,45,"Take recourse to patience and prayer. It may indeed be hard, except for the devoutly humble,"
  2,46,those who are confident that they will meet their Lord and that they will return to Him.
  2,47,"O Children of Israel! Remember My blessing I bestowed upon you, and that I exalted you above the nations (of your age)."
  2,48,"Fear that Day when no soul shall compensate for another. Neither any intercession (of a person who does not have permission to intercede) shall be accepted from it, nor any ransom shall be taken from it, nor shall they be helped (against Allah’s decree)."
